From aedb6a3155401519260b3aae04a9a245aeb9175d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 02:09:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(app): refusal ghost for part-way refusals,
 ghost-aware match sites, ground-aware ghost colour

Generators that refuse part-way now hand back the moves they had built,
as a display-only ghost (GenError::with_ghost_moves over a builder's
moves): 2D contour (control-comp lead and span refusals), bore and
circular (per-hole/ring pass budget), trochoidal slot (level emit,
crossed loops), the 3-D ladder's adaptive level plan, plasma profile
(per-contour, cover/kerf laws, torch spans), probing, turning form and
groove. Every adoption is a map_err on an error path; successful output
is unchanged and the CL/NC goldens are byte-identical. The rest are
listed with their reason in docs/decisions/871-refusal-ghost-rest.md.

cross_spindle::in_world rewrites a Ghosted refusal's sentence, spot and
moves by the spindle shift (dropping the ghost when it cannot carry it);
picks::door_refusal reads a Ghosted refusal's words like the plain one;
body_judged::name_enclosure goes through map_msg so a ghost keeps its
holder words.

The ghost colour takes #698's ground-aware dimming: the dark ground is
unchanged, a light ground fades toward itself, the cutting tone clearing
3:1 on the light viewport in every colour-vision palette.

Fixes #871

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
